# Playwright — Prefer Installed Chrome

Bundled Playwright Chromium often hangs or fails in agent/sandbox environments. **Prefer the user's installed Google Chrome desktop** for local and agent-run e2e.

## Config (already set in `playwright*.config.ts`)

- **Local / agent**: `channel: 'chrome'` with `devices['Desktop Chrome']`
- **CI** (`CI=true`): no channel — use Playwright's bundled Chromium from `playwright install --with-deps chromium`

Do not remove `channel: 'chrome'` from local configs to "fix" agent runs.

## UI changes must update e2e in the same change

CI runs the full Playwright suite. **Do not ship frontend copy / a11y / role changes without updating selectors in the same commit/PR.** This has failed repeatedly when only the app was updated.

When you change any of the following, **grep and update** `tests/e2e/**` (and Maestro `visible`/`tapOn` if applicable) before `yarn verify` / opening a PR:

| UI change | Typical selector breakage |
| --------- | ------------------------- |
| Button / link / menu label | `getByRole('button'\|'link', { name: '…' })` |
| Dialog / MorphingPopover `title` or `aria-label` | `getByRole('dialog', { name: '…' })` |
| `aria-label` on icon buttons | `getByRole('button', { name: '…' })` |
| `data-testid` rename/remove | `getByTestId('…')` |
| Brand / chrome accessible name | Signed-in header **Yowl** button; logged-out FTUE is `sign-in-logo` / `img[name=Yowl]` |
| **Duplicate accessible names** | Adding a second control with the same role+name (e.g. tip-well **Invite someone** next to header invite) → Playwright **strict mode** failures |
| **Substring role names** | `getByRole('heading', { name: 'Suggestions' })` also matches **No suggestions yet** — Playwright name matching is substring unless `{ exact: true }` |

**Do this in the same turn as the UI edit** — not after CI fails:

1. `rg` the old string under `tests/e2e/` and `maestro/`
2. Prefer **stable `data-testid`s** for chrome that will keep changing (menus, dynamic titles, header icon actions). Role+name is fine for stable unique product copy.
3. If a dialog title becomes **dynamic** (e.g. account menu titled with the user's name), stop asserting a fixed dialog name — scope via `getByTestId` / open trigger, or `getByRole('dialog')` without a fixed name.
4. If you add a CTA that **reuses** an existing accessible name, give chrome a `data-testid` and point e2e at that (do not rely on `.first()`).
5. When asserting a short page title that also appears inside empty-state / error headings (e.g. **Suggestions** vs **No suggestions yet**), use `{ exact: true }` or a `data-testid` on the page chrome heading.
6. Run or reason about which specs touch that surface (`notification-prefs`, `group-header`, `a11y-*`, `smoke-production`, `suggestions`, etc.). `smoke-production.spec.ts` is in the CI smoke project against the **PR build**, not only live yowl.us.

## When running e2e

```bash
# Preferred — uses system Chrome via config
yarn test:e2e
yarn verify

# Smoke against production
PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL=https://yowl.us yarn test:e2e --config=playwright.smoke.config.ts
```

## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Action |
| ---- | --- |
| Tests hang at startup | Confirm Google Chrome is installed; do **not** switch to bundled Chromium locally |
| `channel: 'chrome'` not found | Install [Google Chrome](https://www.google.com/chrome/); on macOS it lives in `/Applications/Google Chrome.app` |
| Agent sandbox blocks browser | Request `all` permissions for the test command, not a config change away from Chrome |
| CI failure | Keep `CI=true` path on bundled Chromium; do not set `channel: 'chrome'` in GitHub Actions |
| Brand not found (`name: 'yowl'`) | Signed-in chrome: `getByRole('button', { name: 'Yowl' })`. Logged-out FTUE: `getByTestId('sign-in-logo')` / `getByRole('img', { name: 'Yowl' })` — no header brand button |
| Strict mode: resolved to 2 elements | Duplicate accessible names — scope with `data-testid` (e.g. `group-invite` vs creator tip well). Or substring match: page title **Suggestions** vs empty **No suggestions yet** → add `{ exact: true }` |
| Dialog/button not found after UI polish | You likely changed a label/title without updating e2e — see **UI changes must update e2e** above |

## Avoid locally

- `playwright install chromium` as the first fix for hangs
- Overriding config to force headless bundled Chromium when Chrome is available
- Installing Edge/Firefox projects unless explicitly requested
- Asserting lowercase `yowl` for the header brand — use `getByRole('button', { name: 'Yowl' })` when chrome is shown
- Asserting the header **Yowl** button on logged-out `/` — FTUE is chrome-less (`sign-in-screen`)
- Merging / opening a PR with UI label, dialog-title, or **duplicate-name CTA** changes while leaving `tests/e2e` on the old strings
